From: yifengyou <842056007@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] disk: part_dos: reject GPT protective MBR in test_block_type()

A sector containing a partition entry of type 0xEE (GPT protective
MBR) must not be treated as a valid DOS MBR.  Return -1 immediately
when such an entry is detected, so that the DOS partition driver does
not claim a disk whose first sector belongs to a (possibly malformed)
GPT layout.  This keeps the DOS driver from misinterpreting hybrid or
corrupted GPT disks and lets the EFI partition driver handle them.

Signed-off-by: yifengyou <842056007@qq.com>
---
 disk/part_dos.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/disk/part_dos.c b/disk/part_dos.c
--- a/disk/part_dos.c
+++ b/disk/part_dos.c
@@ -74,9 +74,11 @@ static int test_block_type(unsigned char *buffer)
 	p = (struct dos_partition *)&buffer[DOS_PART_TBL_OFFSET];
 
 	/* Check that the boot indicators are valid and count the partitions. */
 	for (slot = 0; slot < 4; ++slot, ++p) {
+		if (p->sys_ind == 0xee)
+			return -1;
 		if (p->boot_ind != 0 && p->boot_ind != 0x80)
 			break;
 		if (p->sys_ind)
 			++part_count;
 	}
